use but here in new  york it's of course a big topic of  conversation i was looking on twitter  and bill ackman the hedge fund  billionaire has been tweeting about this  he was tweeting that he was watching the  trial and he felt that kyle rittenhouse  was telling the truth and acting in  self-defense his main point though was  that rittenhouse's life is at risk  justice demands a fair trial he says  society would benefit greatly if  politics did not enter the courtroom and  convict innocent people so he's trying  to separate the trial from  political tribes political bias are you  hearing a lot of people talk about  conservatives versus progressives when  you talk to them uh near the courthouse  yeah so you know there are some  signs that are like black lives matter  there is some sort of rhetoric around  that but i think what people here are  trying to also say is that this isn't  necessarily about black lives matter  it's more so about well you know  a white man who was armed  get away  with what he did and if it was a black  man in his situation there might be a  different story so i think that's also  kind of the story that some of these  protesters are trying to to say to the  other side um is that kind is that  conversation right there which is  i think where a lot of the the  discussion comes in among the two sides  of the story when it gets kind of down  to that racial component gotcha gotcha  and one of the folks you talked to  referenced how their riots and and you  haven't seen that happen yet so far  things have been pretty peaceful but i  just wonder do we know how the  authorities in kenosha are preparing uh  for when there is a verdict if there is  any kind of unrest i mean do they have  people standing by  yes so there's definitely like there is  a security presence um you know you'll  see some you know patrol cars around  there's signs saying you can't park here  don't park there um what we do know is  you know the national guard is on  standby um 